# Binary projects live in bin/. This repo is the build environment, so the only
# one it ever carries is the bundled hello_world example: everything else under
# bin/ is ignored, and your own projects can sit right here — workspace members,
# built by the same `cargo x*` commands — without ever showing up in
# `git status`, a `git add -A`, or a PR against rust-mos-env. Keep them in their
# own repo (a nested git repo under bin/ works fine) or a directory of your own.
#
# `/bin/*` ignores each entry rather than `/bin/` itself, so git can still
# descend into the one directory the next line un-ignores.
/bin/*
!/bin/hello_world/

result
result-*
# nix build GC-root symlinks the publish-toolchain-binaries xtask drops in toolchain/
toolchain/gcroot-*

# The C65 ROM xmega65 boots is Cloanto copyright: free to download for your own
# use, NOT redistributable. toolchain/mega65-rom.nix fetches it to your local
# /nix/store and initenv copies it to your Xemu preferences directory — it is
# never meant to live here. Named exactly so a stray copy cannot be committed by
# accident. (Same reason mega65-rom is absent from CACHE_ATTRS in
# xtask/src/publish_toolchain_binaries.rs — pushing it would be redistribution.)
c-65-19910828.rom
MEGA65.ROM
target/
*.bak
**/.idea